       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 1000 mg is five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and I don't see a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **Check with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist.** If a physician really wants a dose above the labeled maximum, they can place or co-sign the order. Pharmacy will probably still want to verify it.\n- **If 1000 mg came from a source such as a note, a sign-out, or a home medication list,** double-check it. It may be a transcription error for 100 mg, or a reported overdose ingestion. An overdose would need a toxicology and poison control evaluation, not a standing order.\n\nI can enter sertraline at a standard dose right now, such as 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily. I can also add a note about titration if you'd like."
      }
